{"ld": 1359, "paper": "HP882", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, to Direct the Department of Transportation to Report Progress Made Toward Implementing Recommendations Based on the 2025 Public Transit Advisory Council Report (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "h-crafts-lydia", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-ankeles-daniel", "s-farrin-bradlee", "h-montell-karen", "s-nangle-timothy", "h-ray-d"], "committee_code": "TRA", "committee_name": "Transportation", "summary": {"text": "This resolve directs the Department of Transportation to develop practices regarding public transit, including:\n\n1. Increasing transparency in the allocation and distribution of funding for public transit operators by publishing annual transit distributions in print form and on a publicly accessible website, including the total amount made available for operations and the amounts allocated to each recipient; 2. Reducing the local match requirement for funding rural public transit operators; and 3. Increasing collaboration and coordination with the Department of Health and Human Services to improve public transit services between health care providers and consumers of the health care providers' services.\n\nThe resolve directs the Department of Transportation, by December 3, 2025, to report on its progress in carrying out this resolve and resulting practices to the Joint Standing Committee on Transportation.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0882&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Finally Passed", "final_disposition": {"label": "Finally Passed", "date": "2025-06-20", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2025-06-20"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1359)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0882&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-302)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?pa